From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: keep the MDIO master enabled when clearing a
 command

After each internal PHY access through management frames,
qca8k_phy_eth_command() writes 0 to MDIO_MASTER_CTRL, which also clears
MDIO_MASTER_EN. On QCA8327, this makes the internal PHYs stop responding
after anything from a few seconds to a few minutes, with or without
traffic. All their registers then read back as 0, through management
frames as well as through MDIO, until the switch is reset. phylib sees
no link and the ports go down for good.

Clearing MDIO_MASTER_EN through the MDIO bus after an access, as
qca8k_mdio_read() and qca8k_mdio_write() do, does not cause this, and
neither do accesses to other registers through management frames.
Keep MDIO_MASTER_EN set in the clear command. Disable the MDIO master
when the switch is removed or shut down, so that the PHYs are reachable
through the external MDC again.

Tested on a TP-Link Archer C7 v2 (QCA8327) with port 0 connected over
SGMII as CPU port. Without this change, the ports died within 1 to 10
minutes in each of 5 runs, also with "net: dsa: qca8k: fail mgmt
Ethernet MDIO access on busy wait errors" applied. With it, they
survived 90 minutes of bidirectional traffic, with the internal PHYs
accessed through management frames.

Fixes: 2cd548566384 ("net: dsa: qca8k: add support for phy read/write with mgmt Ethernet")
Assisted-by: opencode:big-pickle
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -630,7 +630,7 @@ qca8k_phy_eth_command(struct qca8k_priv
 {
 	struct sk_buff *write_skb, *clear_skb, *read_skb;
 	struct qca8k_mgmt_eth_data *mgmt_eth_data;
-	u32 write_val, clear_val = 0, val;
+	u32 write_val, clear_val = QCA8K_MDIO_MASTER_EN, val;
 	struct net_device *mgmt_conduit;
 	int ret, ret1;
 	bool ack;
@@ -684,7 +684,7 @@ qca8k_phy_eth_command(struct qca8k_priv
 	 * 1. Send mdio master packet
 	 * 2. Busy Wait for mdio master command
 	 * 3. Get the data if we are reading
-	 * 4. Reset the mdio master (even with error)
+	 * 4. Clear the command bits while keeping the mdio master selected
 	 */
 	mutex_lock(&mgmt_eth_data->mutex);
 
@@ -2239,6 +2239,16 @@ qca8k_sw_probe(struct mdio_device *mdiod
 	return dsa_register_switch(priv->ds);
 }
 
+static void qca8k_mdio_master_disable(struct qca8k_priv *priv)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = regmap_clear_bits(priv->regmap, QCA8K_MDIO_MASTER_CTRL,
+				QCA8K_MDIO_MASTER_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_warn(priv->dev, "failed to disable mdio master: %d\n", ret);
+}
+
 static void
 qca8k_sw_remove(struct mdio_device *mdiodev)
 {
@@ -2252,6 +2262,7 @@ qca8k_sw_remove(struct mdio_device *mdio
 		qca8k_port_set_status(priv, i, 0);
 
 	dsa_unregister_switch(priv->ds);
+	qca8k_mdio_master_disable(priv);
 }
 
 static void qca8k_sw_shutdown(struct mdio_device *mdiodev)
@@ -2262,6 +2273,7 @@ static void qca8k_sw_shutdown(struct mdi
 		return;
 
 	dsa_switch_shutdown(priv->ds);
+	qca8k_mdio_master_disable(priv);
 
 	dev_set_drvdata(&mdiodev->dev, NULL);
 }
